        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people who train, the Theragun Prime (6th Gen) or the Hyperice Hypervolt 3 is the massage gun to buy</strong>
            — the Prime for its published 16 mm stroke and tough body, the Hypervolt for its lower
            price, quieter motor by its maker's figure and fuller set of heads. Choose the Theragun
            Mini if portability decides whether you use one, the Relief if full-size guns feel too
            intense, the Ekrin B37 for its warranty and battery, and the RENPHO Active+ as a cheap
            trial.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, choose by amplitude, weight and comfort rather than stall force, use light
